@page "/teaching/csharp/3-generics-and-collections"
@inject CourseBook CourseBook;

<CourseModuleIntroduction Module="@CourseBook.CSharpCourse["generics-and-collections"]">
    <MudText GutterBottom="true">
        We introduce more advanced types in .NET in form of generics.
        The overall goal is to introduce the basic BCL collections and how they work.
        To do that we also need to talk about equality. We also introduce tuples and
        deconstruction. In this module we will learn:
    </MudText>
        
    <OList Class="d-block my-4" Padding="false">
        <ListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ChevronRight">defining indexers;</ListItem>
        <ListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ChevronRight">generic types and methods;</ListItem>
        <ListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ChevronRight">how nullability interacts with generics;</ListItem>
        <ListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ChevronRight">referential and structural equality;</ListItem>
        <ListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ChevronRight">custom equality;</ListItem>
        <ListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ChevronRight"><Code>GetHashCode</Code>;</ListItem>
        <ListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ChevronRight"><Code>IEquatable&lt;T&gt;</Code>;</ListItem>
        <ListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ChevronRight"><Code>IComparable&lt;T&gt;</Code>;</ListItem>
        <ListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ChevronRight">basic collections in the BCL;</ListItem>
        <ListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ChevronRight">comparer types <Code>IEqualityComparer&lt;T&gt;</Code> and <Code>IComparer&lt;T&gt;</Code>;</ListItem>
        <ListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ChevronRight">tuples;</ListItem>
        <ListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ChevronRight">deconstruction;</ListItem>
        <ListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ChevronRight">nested types.</ListItem>
    </OList>
</CourseModuleIntroduction>

